    {
      "id": "1ykasoj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Biomolecules comprise carbohydrates, proteins, lipids, and nucleic acids, serving as the building blocks of life.",
        "Carbohydrate metabolism covers glycolysis, the citric acid cycle, glycogenesis, and glycogenolysis.",
        "Proteins are broken down into amino acids, with excess nitrogen processed through the urea cycle.",
        "Enzymes function as biological catalysts, significantly reducing activation energy for cellular reactions.",
        "Vitamins and minerals serve as critical cofactors and micronutrients for physiological stability.",
        "Strict regulation of arterial pH between 7.35 and 7.45 maintains acid-base homeostasis."
      ],
      "id": "5s7k95r"
    },
